# Arrival at the Moonstone Mask

## Scene summary (from gm-assist, verbatim)

#### The party enters the luxurious Moonstone Mask to return a long-lost statue, only to learn of a tragic death.

- The party arrives at the Moonstone Mask, a high-end inn floating above Neverwinter on a tethered earthmote.
- Valphine's passive perception of 17 notices that "everybody here is very... all the waitstaff is very pretty."
- The DM describes the staff as dressed in "sheer black," all wearing moonstone-lined half-masks alongside amulets.
- A staff member recognizes Vukradin and says: "Oh my. Vukradin, you've come to our establishment."
- When Vukradin asks for Elara, the DM describes: "Her eyes suddenly grow cold."
- The staff member informs the party that Lady Elara Meliamne, the intended recipient of the statue, was killed eight days prior in a "catastrophic, catastrophic, spectacular and bloody disaster" during a festival.
- The staff member says Elara's death was "beyond the ability to be raised. Even if her brother did want to raise her." *[Quoted verbatim. The table used "brother"/"his sister" throughout this scene; per campaign canon Cassian is Elara's **cousin**. Quotes are left as spoken; narration uses cousin.]*
- The staff member notes that Lord Neverember "has declared that the death of Elara was a tragic accident, and that we were all to mourn her passing and move on."
- The party is directed to Lord Cassian, Elara's cousin, who is currently at the inn.
- The staff member mistakes Brewbarry for someone merely dressed in the popular "Brewbarry aesthetic." She says: "Oh my, I didn't realize that the Brewbarry aesthetic was something that people would wear in the Moonstone Mask... the whole... I always thought the Brewbarry aesthetic was... the Uthgardian aesthetic was anti-Moonstone Mask." She assumes Brewbarry is "somebody who's dressed like you, not actually a Uthgarian Barbarian... Brewbarry."
- Brewbarry doesn't mind and gets a "very large pouring of something that tastes amazing."
- The staff member looks at Valphine and says: "Oh, you're a blessing upon me."

## Verbatim moments

**[The Approach — Docks and the Common Chord]**
- The party crosses the Protector's Enclave — "a very rich, neighborhood, lots of, what's the word I'm looking for? Signs of the rich and powerful" — and steps out onto the dock area, which immediately becomes "grungy."
- They pass Vukradin's old haunt, the Common Chord, on the right.
- Brewbarry rolls an Insight check and gets a minus 1; the GM rules he notices nothing.

**GM** — *on the Common Chord's past*
> "What you remember of the Common Chord was, it was kind of a desperate place."
> "Right? Like, nobody went there."

**GM** — *on Vukradin's old employment there*
> "and, you know, which was… may explain why you were able to find employment there. And by employment, I mean they were… they would periodically let you play, and then throw you out. And not pay you."

**Vukradin** — *defending his old business model*
> "Well, I didn't get perfect ratings, and the deal was that, you know, if you weren't completely satisfied, you could have your money back."

**GM**
> "Yes. Yes, this created a problem."

**GM** — *offering a detour*
> "But what you do notice is that the Common Chord, you kind of… do either of you want to go check it out, or look at it?"

**Vukradin** / **Soma**
> "No, no, we're returning the statue. We have to stay focused."
> "No side questing today."

**Vukradin**
> "Lord, Ser Kaelen told me I needed to do this."
> "Finally do it. I'm doing it."

**GM** — *the Common Chord's current status*
> "But you do… but you do remember that the Common Chord was your old hangout, and you do also remember that when the… when you arrived in the city, the guard said that he would love for Vukradin to get him tickets at the hardest place to get a ticket to go eat."
> "which is now the Common Chord."

**Brewbarry** — *on the ale he remembers*
> "Yes, all I remember is a shitty ale. Good music, but shitty ale."

**GM**
> "Actually, no, that was when… to be fair, I don't know Brewbarry. Canonically speaking, it's when you arrived in Neverwinter that you discovered that ale could be good."

**Brewbarry**
> "Yeah, but now I know better."
> "It was, like… piss."

**GM**
> "Your standards have improved, alright. Okay, so you arrive at the Moonstone Mask."

**[The Earthmote — Geography of the Floating Inn]**
- The GM pulls up the district description of Neverwinter's three tethered earthmotes.
- The Moonstone Mask sits on a floating earthmote connected to the docks of the Protector's Enclave.

**GM** — *reading the lore*
> "One of the most enchanting city features of the city of Neverwinter is its three floating, large earth motes."
> "Right? The spell plague of 1385 caused chunks of Neverwinter, as well as other areas all over Toril, to rise up and begin floating away. Industrious residents of Neverwinter were able to tether a few of these earth motes."
> "and prevent them from ultimately flying off into the Sword Coast."

**GM** — *reading the Moonstone Mask entry*
> "The Moonstone Mask is a large inn that sits on a floating earth mote connected to the docks of the Protector's Enclave section of Neverwinter. It is regarded by many as Neverwinter's finest, most luxurious inn. The locale is named for the half-masks worn by all the staff, which are lined with glowing Moonstones."

**Vukradin** — *asking how thick the earthmotes are*
> "Right? Because it's, like, it's like land floating in the sky, right? So there's got to be some amount of… Yes, it's, yes."
> "all these buildings, right? Like, they have basements, they have catacombs, they have, you know, buried coffins, graveyards, like, that all requires some amount of depth."

**GM** — *ruling on the shape*
> "Right, okay, so great question. So what you notice is that it's asymm… it's like the middle part is a lot deeper than the edge part."
> "So it's not a… It's not a flat cutoff."
> "Right? So, if there were any catacombs and dungeons, they would fit naturally into that cone area."

**Soma**
> "It's like a cone, yeah."
> "I have to put the cemeteries in the middle of town."
> "Right. Sorry, in the middle of the island."

**GM** — *on what the Moonstone Mask is for*
> "A place where the rich and the powerful go to chill out and relax."

**Brewbarry**
> "Thinking, eyes wide shut here."

**GM** — *on Vukradin's history with the place*
> "Vukradin would know about this place if he had been bothering to listen to anything other than his music at the time."

**Vukradin**
> "They always snubbed me. They're never… they're never willing to host me."

**GM**
> "To be fair, there were very few places that were willing to snub you."

**Vukradin**
> "Yeah, but this place was not willing to host me."

**GM**
> "No, it was not. But you kind of thought they were beneath you. I thought, well…"

**Soma**
> "You snubbed them before they could snub you."

**Vukradin**
> "There you go, there you go."
> "He's snubbed by these rich assholes."

**[Arrival — Perception and the Staff]**
- The GM calls for insight/investigation checks from Valphine and Vukradin.
- Vukradin rolls poorly and notices nothing.
- Valphine's passive perception is 17.

**GM** — *setting the scene*
> "The Moonstone Mask, as you, as you arrive, you discover the Moonstone Mask's accommodations and unparalleled views,"
> "are astonishing, but… Roll, Valphine, roll some insight checks, or perception checks."

**GM** — *what Valphine's 17 passive perception plus insight reveals*
> "Alright, so, I mean, combined with your passive perception and your insight, what you do notice is that everybody here is very… all the waitstaff is very pretty."

**Vukradin**
> "I mean, that makes sense, right? It's a high-end establishment, but they're not gonna have ugly people."

**Soma**
> "Beauty is in the eye of the beholder, come on."

**GM** — *on the range of the staff*
> "Yeah, yes. I mean, you know, for… satisfying a wide variety of aesthetics for pretty…"
> "And not all female, it's, you know, a mix of genders, species, it's, you know…"

**Soma**
> "I'm saying there's someone for Soma."

**Vukradin**
> "Someone for everybody."

**GM** — *the uniform*
> "There, all the Moonstone staff are dressed in sheer black, also… each also wearing the inn's namesake's masks and an amulet."

**Vukradin** — *fishing for a plot hook*
> "What does the amulet look like?"

**GM**
> "Doesn't, doesn't really say. I cannot."

**Vukradin**
> "Okay, so it's not, no, not plot."
> "Not an amulet of Talos."

**GM**
> "No, no, there's no… it's not an amulet of some dark god."

**Soma**
> "That we know of."

**Valphine**
> "This is an amulet of a so-called Good God? Weak God."

**[The Main Hall]**

**GM** — *describing the interior*
> "You arrive in the main hall."
> "And the inn features a large, warm, and inviting floor dining room."
> "It serves as a comfortable lounge with an impressive hearth."
> "The rest of the first floor is taken up by kitchens dedicating to preparing haute cuisine for the inn's many guests. A grand, spiraling stair case leads up from the dining room to the guest rooms above. The atmosphere of the dining room is generally relaxed, with polite conversation occurring throughout."

**GM** — *the party's first impression on the room*
> "And as you're sort of sitting there, looking very much uncouth."
> "And so seemingly out of place."
> "Someone approaches you, a member of the staff approaches you."

**[The Staff Member — Recognition]**

**Staff member** — *recognising Vukradin*
> "Oh my."
> "Vukradin, you've come to our establishment."

**Vukradin**
> "Hi."

**Soma** / **Brewbarry** — *OOC over the top*
> "Hey, baby."
> "Yeah, we expect free drinks."

**Vukradin**
> "We're looking for someone, maybe you can help us, since you… since you seem to know who I am."

**Staff member**
> "Oh, well, of course, for you, Mr. Vukradin, anything you would like."

**Vukradin**
> "We're looking for Elara."

**GM** — *narration*
> "Her eyes suddenly grow cold."

**Vukradin**
> "So is that a 'I don't know Elara'?"

**Staff member**
> "didn't you hear?"
> "He's dead."

**Soma**
> "Oh, fiddle sticks."

**Vukradin**
> "What happened?"

**Staff member**
> "Well, there was a big party."
> "And it ended in a catastrophic, catastrophic, spectacular and bloody disaster."
> "But, I have good news."
> "Her brother is over there. Maybe you want to go talk to him."

**Vukradin**
> "Definitely. But tell me more about this bloody attack, like, what happened?"

**Staff member**
> "Well, there was a festival. She was throwing an event."
> "And during the event, something happened. I wasn't there, so I wouldn't know."

**Vukradin**
> "Oh, okay."
> "You just heard, but…"

**Staff member**
> "Yes, and she passed away. It was quite tragic, even beyond the ability to be raised."
> "Even if her brother did want to raise her."

**Valphine**
> "What do you suspect happened?"

**Soma**
> "Also, you mentioned her brother did not want her up?"

**Valphine** — *rephrasing to something the NPC will answer*
> "Or maybe an easier question. What do people say happened?"

**Staff member** — *the competing rumours*
> "So what happened was, there wasn't… there was supposed to be a party, and at this party, there was a group of people who showed up."
> "And, to be quite honest, it's not quite clear. Everybody has a very different version of the facts."
> "Some people say it was, you know, some love affair that went sideways. Other people say it was a raid. Yet another group says it was some magical spell that went sideways. To be quite honest, everybody has a very different version of the facts."

**Staff member** — *the official line*
> "but Dagult Neverember has declared that the death of Elara was a tragic accident, and that we were all to mourn her passing and move on."

**Valphine**
> "Thank you for explaining. That was very helpful."

**Vukradin**
> "Plenty of things happen."

**[The Brewbarry Aesthetic Misunderstanding]**
- The staff member offers Vukradin and Soma drinks, then turns to Brewbarry.

**Staff member** — *to Brewbarry*
> "oh my, I didn't realize that the Brewbarry aesthetic was something that people would wear in the masked mask."

**Brewbarry**
> "To what now? Where are the drinks?"

**Vukradin** — *OOC egging him on*
> "You should show her the robes, man."

**Staff member**
> "yes! You know, I don't mean to be rude, but, like, the whole… I always thought the Brewbarry aesthetic was… the Uthgardian aesthetic was anti-masked mask."

**Brewbarry**
> "Bless you. Do you want to see my robes?"
> "I'll give you a special."

**GM** — *reminding the table of the fashion situation*
> "just in case you've forgotten."
> "People in Neverwinter seem to be wearing your clothes… seem to be dressing up like you."

**Brewbarry**
> "I haven't noticed. I don't know."
> "Doesn't everybody dress like me?"

**GM** — *clarifying the joke*
> "Yeah, okay, right. Yeah, so I just want to be clear, she's assuming you're somebody who's dressed like you, not actually a Uthgardian Barbarian… Brewbarry."

**Brewbarry** — *unbothered*
> "You're saying this, like, than me finding free drinks around here, you know, like I care."
> "I don't think Brewbarry minds at all."

**Staff member** — *reading it as fashion commentary*
> "well, this is very daring of you. Maybe it's… oh, I know what it is. You're trying to… this is a counterstatement to the statement, I love it."

**GM** — *the reward*
> "And she gives you a very large pouring of something that tastes amazing."

**Brewbarry**
> "Finally. You're… now you're making sense. Thank you."

**[Valphine's Glowing Eyes]**

**Staff member** — *to Valphine*
> "Oh, you're a blessing upon me."

**GM** — *reminding the table why*
> "Right, remember you got the glowing eyes, you know, everybody kind of thinks you're the avatar of the good god Lathander."

**Vukradin**
> "He is the avatar of the good god of the Lathander, but it's…"

**GM**
> "Your eyeball blessing is kind of like, you know, and I'll do…"

**Valphine**
> "The swivel eyes thing."

- The staff member points the party toward Lord Cassian Meliamne.

**Vukradin**
> "Alright, we're gonna go talk to the brother."
